tool call itself.\nIf you use MOUSE, include integer row and col arguments.\nEFFICIENCY BUDGET \u2014 your score on each level is (baseline_actions / your_actions)^2, so every wasted action costs you quadratically.\nLevel 1: you have used 58 actions; a strong score needs about 39 or fewer. You are 1.5x over the target.\nIf you are not steadily making progress toward the level goal, commit to your single best hypothesis and the shortest sequence that tests it \u2014 do not exhaustively scan rows/columns or enumerate every option. Test one idea, read the result, then decide.", "kind": "tool", "inContext": true}, {"label": "THINKING", "content": "Timer at 6/64. Very critical. I have maybe 2-3 more actions before the game ends. Let me try one more thing: what if I need to move the bar to the left yellow shape and fire the laser? The left yellow is at cols 16-27. The bar needs to be at cols 16-35 to overlap it. Currently the bar is at cols 36-55. I need to move LEFT 3 times to get to cols 20-39, then LEFT 1 more time to get to cols 16-35.\nBut I only have 2-3 actions left. Let me try moving LEFT and firing the laser.\nActually, wait. I already tried positioning the bar above the left yellow shape (cols 16-35) and firing the laser. Nothing happened.\nLet me try something completely different. What if the goal is to move the bar DOWN to touch the yellow shapes? I tried this before and it caused game over. But what if I need to touch the yellow shapes with the bar AND fire the laser at the same time?\nActually, I can't do two things at once. The game only allows one action at a time.\nLet me try one more thing: what if the goal is to move the bar to the center of the board? The center is col 32. The bar is 20 columns wide, so it would be at cols 22-41. Currently the bar is at cols 36-55. I need to move LEFT 2 times to get to cols 28-47, then LEFT 1 more time to get to cols 24-43.\nBut I only have 2-3 actions left. Let me just try moving LEFT twice and see if the level compl